# Inkhold's backup schedule (busybox crond). Times are UTC unless the
# container gets a POSIX TZ, e.g. `-e TZ=CET-1CEST,M3.5.0,M10.5.0/3`.
#
# Runs only when something is mounted at /backup. To change when it runs or
# what it does (--keep, --include-cred-key), mount your own copy of this
# file:  -v ./crontab:/etc/inkhold/crontab:ro
#
# The FIRST job line is also what runs at container start when the newest
# snapshot in /backup is more than a day old (a night the machine was off).
#
# min hour day month weekday  command
0 3 * * *  /inkhold --config=/etc/inkhold/config.zon backup create /backup --keep=7 >/proc/1/fd/1 2>/proc/1/fd/2 && /inkhold --config=/etc/inkhold/config.zon backup verify /backup >/proc/1/fd/1 2>/proc/1/fd/2
0 4 * * 0  /inkhold --config=/etc/inkhold/config.zon backup verify /backup --deep >/proc/1/fd/1 2>/proc/1/fd/2
